WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.350
Imagine a friend asks you:

2
00:00:01.350 --> 00:00:03.760
«Qu'est-ce que tu ferais»…
«si tu gagnais au loto

3
00:00:03.760 --> 00:00:06.100
?» What would you do if you won?

4
00:00:06.100 --> 00:00:07.940
A house? A trip?

5
00:00:07.940 --> 00:00:11.220
In English, would is its own little word.

6
00:00:11.220 --> 00:00:12.420
I would buy.

7
00:00:12.420 --> 00:00:13.640
I would travel.

8
00:00:13.640 --> 00:00:16.240
So which French word means would?

9
00:00:16.240 --> 00:00:17.540
And notice this.

10
00:00:17.540 --> 00:00:19.740
In English you say if I won,

11
00:00:19.740 --> 00:00:21.530
not if I would win.

12
00:00:21.530 --> 00:00:23.520
Does French follow the same ban?

13
00:00:23.520 --> 00:00:25.710
So how do you say what you would do,

14
00:00:25.710 --> 00:00:28.350
and why does if never take would?

15
00:00:28.350 --> 00:00:32.060
In this mission, you'll discover
where French keeps its would.

16
00:00:32.060 --> 00:00:36.310
Then you'll test «si» sentences
on a timeline in the lab,

17
00:00:36.310 --> 00:00:38.640
likely plans and imagined ones.

18
00:00:38.640 --> 00:00:42.920
Your mission: work out how to answer
the lottery question in French.
